stop asks the daemon to exit and waits until the socket stops answering.
A socket file left behind by a crashed daemon is removed so the next start
is clean.

Usage:
  ley daemon stop [flags]

Examples:
  ley daemon stop
  ley daemon stop && ley daemon start   # restart

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for stop

Global Flags:
      --bin string      path to the leylined binary
      --json            machine output: proto3 JSON (NDJSON for streams)
      --log string      daemon log file (default: ~/Library/Logs/Leyline/leylined.log)
      --socket string   daemon socket path (default: user daemon UDS, $LEYLINE_SOCKET)
